  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "UA_SecureChannelManager_deleteMembers",
    "file": "open62541/src/server/ua_securechannel_manager.c",
    "description": "Heap-use-after-free during server teardown: secure-channel entries can be freed earlier via delayed callback removeSecureChannelCallback (scheduled by removeSecureChannel and executed in UA_Server_run_shutdown/processDelayedCallbacks), but UA_SecureChannelManager_deleteMembers later iterates cm->channels and calls UA_SecureChannel_deleteMembersCleanup on an entry that was already freed. The manager keeps/uses a stale channel list entry, causing UAF when traversing channel->sessions in UA_SecureChannel_deleteMembersCleanup.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_binary_message, crafted binary messages create a session/channel, then trigger a path that schedules secure-channel removal (delayed callback) before final teardown. Harness calls UA_Server_run_shutdown() (executes delayed callbacks and frees channel entry) and then UA_Server_delete() (calls UA_SecureChannelManager_deleteMembers). If the channel entry is still reachable from manager teardown logic after delayed free, cleanup runs twice on freed memory, producing UAF."
  },
